{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1378109-mage-wants-to-transform-into-a-living-ball-of-fire-at-a-later-date","id":1378109,"title":"Mage wants to transform into a living ball of fire at a later date","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-02T17:34:04-07:00","id":1378109,"title":"Mage wants to transform into a living ball of fire at a later date","content":"The character wanted to be able to transform himself into a ball of fire, he has All spheres of three dots or higher<br /> <br /> he is getting surrounded by vampires at some future time, and wants to literally transformed himself into a ball of fire at a moment when he is physically attacked grappled or incapacitated. Can he do this and what spheres will he need?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T18:09:09-07:00","id":1378125,"title":"","content":"Life 4/forces 3/prime 2. Welcome to paradox town and blowing quintessence to keep the agg train going.<br /> <br /> But his paradigm has to support such a thing, remember that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T05:05:33-07:00","id":1378229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1378109-mage-wants-to-transform-into-a-living-ball-of-fire-at-a-later-date?p=1378125#post1378125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Life 4/forces 3/prime 2. Welcome to paradox town and blowing quintessence to keep the agg train going.<br /> <br /> But his paradigm has to support such a thing, remember that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires already take aggravated damage from fire, so the mage in question won't need to spend quintessence to change Lethal&gt;Agg like they normally do. Same with silver for werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T06:41:12-07:00","id":1378252,"title":"","content":"Even more so. Fire does aggravated damage automatically, not just to vampires but to everyone. <br /> <br /> M20 page 436 details fire damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T07:02:42-07:00","id":1378256,"title":"","content":"Vulcan's Hammer from the Order of Hermes' tradition book<br /> <br /> <br /> Vulcan\u2019s Hammer<br /> [Forces \u2022\u2022\u2022, Life \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Matter \u2022\u2022\u2022]<br /> There are times when subtlety is called for. Vulcan\u2019s<br /> Hammer is not a rote for those times. This enchantment<br /> transforms a mage into a living weapon of iron and flame. The<br /> effect is most often focused through a statuette of the mage in<br /> question, sculpted from iron-rich clay and hardened under<br /> intense heat. Over the course of working the clay, the mage<br /> scribes and then kneads her True Name into it 10 separate times,<br /> thus concealing the truth of her identity within it and making<br /> the statuette a conduit through which her own living Pattern<br /> may be affected. (Understandably, an Order mage does well to<br /> carefully protect the focus for this Effect, as it does contain<br /> information about her innermost being, through which all<br /> manner of deleterious magics might be worked against her.)<br /> While in the (grossly vulgar) shape of Vulcan\u2019s Hammer,<br /> the average mage weighs in at just about a ton and is wreathed in<br /> flames of up to 1000 degrees in temperature. Needless to say,<br /> there is not much that can stand before the assault, or even the<br /> close passing, of such a juggernaut (therefore, beware before<br /> using this rote on wooden floors, near gas stations or in a mine<br /> shaft, among many other places\u2026).<br /> System: Vulcan\u2019s Hammer grants the following changes to<br /> Attributes: +3 Strength, -2 Dexterity (to a minimum of 1), +4<br /> Stamina. The mage automatically fails all Social Attribute rolls,<br /> except those involving intimidation, against any Sleeper who is not<br /> aware and accepting of the mage\u2019s Awakened nature. She inflicts<br /> normal Forces damage on those who come in physical contact with<br /> her while in this state. By adding Prime 2 to the rote, the mage can<br /> deal aggravated damage with hand-to-hand attacks, soak aggravated<br /> damage normally and inflict aggravated damage on any who<br /> come in physical contact with her. While in this shape, she is<br /> immune to phenomena that specifically target organic beings, is<br /> subject to phenomena that affect normal iron (save for Prime 4<br /> Flames of Purification, as she is still a living thing) and is a walking<br /> Paradox magnet. Naturally, this Effect is always vulgar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T16:02:39-07:00","id":1378868,"title":"","content":"ok so life 4, forces 3 for sure.<br /> <br /> how about to make this happen at a later date, specifically when attacked or some other circumstance comes to pass?<br /> <br /> what does this aspect of the effect require?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T16:58:59-07:00","id":1378881,"title":"","content":"You need Time 4 to &quot;hang&quot; an effect until a later time and Entropy (I believe 3) to have it keyed to a specific circumstance","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T00:24:53-07:00","id":1378944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1378109-mage-wants-to-transform-into-a-living-ball-of-fire-at-a-later-date?p=1378881#post1378881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You need Time 4 to &quot;hang&quot; an effect until a later time and Entropy (I believe 3) to have it keyed to a specific circumstance</div> </div> </div> </div>anyway you can get me a reference on that.<br /> <br /> hope im not asking to much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T06:53:31-07:00","id":1378982,"title":"","content":"The M20 Core book list Time 4 as an effect trigger (and all other triggers) in the Sphere description. Entropy is detailed as a circumstance trigger in HDYDT page 113. I'm not sure where Entropy is described this way in M20 Core but both these spheres have been how you delay effects for as long as I can remember. So it's not like Entropy doing so is new to HDYDT.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":987,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","user":"Tuch","date":".  Spelling 04-06-2020, 09:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T00:13:03-07:00","id":1379421,"title":"","content":"Tuch is correct. Time 4 (to &quot;hang&quot; an Effect for later) + Entropy 3 (to key the activation on a predetermined trigger) has always been how it's done. You could do Time 4 alone if you want to set a specific duration for the Effect to lie dormant, but context-specific ones require Entropy 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}